AB  - This paper analyzes the rise of smart cities, particularly focusing on China's advancements and global export of smart city technologies. It highlights the benefits of smart cities while also addressing the potential risks to individual privacy, data security, and national security. The study examines China's approach to smart city development, including the use of AI, facial recognition, and social credit systems. It also investigates the export of Chinese smart city systems to various countries and the associated allegations of spreading authoritarian norms and values. Finally, it discusses the development of smart cities in Israel and the need for a comprehensive national plan to manage risks related to privacy, data security, and cyber protection.
