AB  - This report by ARTICLE 19 and Digital Rights Collective investigates the procurement and deployment of Closed-Circuit Television (CCTV) systems in Myanmar, focusing on Mandalay, Yangon, and Naypyidaw. It highlights concerns about transparency, accountability, and the human rights implications of CCTV infrastructure, especially in the context of the 2021 military coup. The study reveals how CCTV systems, often procured through opaque processes with significant involvement from companies like Huawei, are becoming the foundation for mass surveillance and AI-driven technologies. The report emphasizes the lack of data protection frameworks and the erosion of freedoms of expression, privacy, and assembly due to the expanding surveillance network. Recommendations are provided for the military junta and private sector to ensure rights-respecting smart city development.
