AB  - This statement from the Mines Advisory Group (MAG) addresses the humanitarian harm caused by explosive weapons in populated areas. It welcomes revisions to the draft political declaration but proposes amendments to articles 3.5 and 4.2. The suggested changes emphasize the importance of risk education alongside clearance efforts and call for improved data collection, sharing, and public availability regarding the effects of explosive weapons, including types, locations, and civilian casualties. MAG advocates for broader data collection beyond 'explosive weapons with wide area effects' and clarification of state obligations in partnered military operations.
