AB  - Along with artificial intelligence and autonomous cars, drones, which can be called the core of the fourth industrial revolution, are expected to bring about innovative changes in our lives. In general, drones are classified according to the purpose of use and the characteristics of the aircraft, and are widely used around us for military, commercial, and civilian operating purposes in accordance with the existing classification criteria.The rapid development of science and technology is reshaping the human life and living environment in the city, a human living space, which is represented by smart cities. In the new converged city of Smart City, drones are a major vehicle for intelligent transportation systems, but with existing classification standards, questions are being raised to accommodate new roles.This research conducted a comprehensive analysis of the major classification criteria for drones in developed countries and based on them, it was intended to present appropriate concepts, classification criteria in future smart cities.In future innovative cities, scientific development will digitalize existing human lives and the way of life, and the fourth industrial revolution will further accelerate, reshaping the innovation infrastructure of various cultures, economies and transport within the city. It would be more reasonable to consider these circumstances and to classify drones, in view of future developments, and more reasonable to consider the changes that the fourth industrial revolution will bring to our society.Subsequent studies also require a new perspective on the areas of security, utilization of future drones, and security that this study did not address. Based on these studies, there should be active discussions on preparing regulations for the operation of drones, legislating and regulating drones, and fostering new industries.
