AB  - Today, in major countries around the world, Mega City with a population of over 10 million is selected as factors influencing each country's competitiveness, and efforts are being made to foster mega-cities. In particular, the technology of the 4th Industrial Revolution has enriched the life of Mega City. As a result, Mega City is attracting the surrounding population, and through this, it is developing into a center of politics, economy and culture. Meanwhile, the emergence of this Mega City is expected to create a new threat, as seen in the corona crisis. The characteristics of an ICT-based networked smart city, a city with a population of over 10 million, will face new threats from an existing, potential, transnational and non-military perspective. In this paper, we discuss the characteristics of Mega City in terms of the structure of Mega City, the implementation of the fourth industrial revolution technology, and the system of system, and presents analysis in terms of presence, potential, transnational, non-military and countermeasures of new threats in terms of prevention, preparedness, response and recovery to be faced in the future.
