TI  - System for performing false positive detection,            root cause analysis of security attack problems            associated with different types of systems and            remediation of problems, has processor for implementing            remediation in response to parameters associated with            simulation falling within desired parameters
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a processor for providing an                output indicating that a subsystem is exhibiting                abnormal behavior from an orchestrator (21a) to an                artificial intelligence system that is capable of                detecting abnormal behavior. The processor                simulates a result of implementing remediation in                response to determination of the artificial                intelligence system, and implements the remediation                based on parameters associated with the simulation                falling within the desired parameters. A memory is                coupled to the processor, and provides the                processor with instructions.
                    USE - System for performing false positive                detection, root cause analysis of security attack                problems associated with different types of systems                and remediation of the security attack problems.                Uses include but are not limited to financial                systems, health care systems, national security                information such as security clearance information,                criminal investigation systems, control systems for                critical infrastructure such as electrical grids                and water/waste systems, telecommunication systems,                Internet of Things (IoT), smart city systems, smart                nation systems and smart highway systems.
                    ADVANTAGE - The orchestrator has access to real time data                about a subsystem with which the subsystem is                associated, so that use of distributed                orchestrators overcomes all scale problems                including the data volume overload problem as each                orchestrator only has local data to analyze and can                do extremely quickly. The system makes analysis and                decisions based on the data in umbrella model so as                to overcome complexity problem of different                non-compatible components/subsystems and layers of                legacy/future technologies.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for: (1) a                method for performing false positive detection,                root cause analysis of security attack problems                associated with different types of systems and                remediation of the security attack problems; (2) a                computer program product storing instructions for                performing false positive detection, root cause                analysis of security attack problems associated                with different types of systems and remediation of                the security attack problems.9
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a system                to provide false positive filtering.101User102Access control system103Behavioral analysis system121-126Orchestrators150 System for implementing automated                behavioral analysis process
